{"id": "unknown-2026-09-08-004", "date": "2026-09-08", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 9, "week": 37, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Memory prices are hitting OLED volumes, not OLED design wins", "content": "<p>The mood around AMOLED in 2026 has been gloomy, and with reason. Rising memory prices have squeezed handset bills of materials, the broader phone market is soft - analysts expect AMOLED smartphone shipments to decline around 7% in 2026, the first decline for AMOLEDs in many years.</p><img data-entity-uuid=\"e0e8c3a6-a98c-4c5f-8da5-67e5e2b19c32\" data-entity-type=\"file\" src=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/default/files/inline-images/OLED-smartphone-design-share-changes-2021-2026-OLED-Info.png\" ", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/memory-prices-are-hitting-oled-volumes-not-oled-design-wins", "type": "rss"}]}
